From: HiBreak Pro Color <hibreak@localhost>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 18:16:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HiBreak Pro Color: Android 16 frameworks/base essentials

Ported from the validated 22.2 baseline; keep the existing kernel/vendor.
FlatWindowBorder: whole-pixel edge (round(density), 2px at 300dpi), ink from the window theme's colorForeground instead of the night mode, path outlines (per-corner or top-only shapes) stroked inside their clip; GradientDrawable reports four equal corner radii as a round-rect outline (M3 popup and context menus). Toast frames carry their own edge. With flat windows SystemUI dialogs launched from a view (QS tiles, footer, media) open as plain floating windows, so the window border frames them and the source keeps drawing. Power menu: no tint over the outlined list and the now outlined button circles.
Dropped strokes on resources the active Android 16 paths do not use: the legacy media output and small-radius volume backgrounds, and the in-framework chooser background (IntentResolver draws its own).
The SettingsLib v36 surface colours and theme backgrounds moved to frameworks_base/0002 (SettingsLib E-Ink containers).
---

